    <bpmn:task id="task_w8q788dp" name="Relayout plan as vertical flow" dai:notes="2026-11-07: The 4-row layout made arrows wrap back across rows. Changed to one top-to-bottom column, with bigger gaps between phases and the phase labels on the left. Saved edges are all straight vertical lines.&#10;MCP findings:&#10;(1) A new bpmn:SubProcess comes in at 100x80, and moving a child into it doesn&#39;t resize the container or move the child. There&#39;s no op to set a container&#39;s size.&#10;(2) move with parent &#34;&#34; or null is accepted but does nothing. There&#39;s no way to move a task back to the top level.&#10;(3) Deleting a container also deletes its children, with no warning. &#39;Choose rendering stack&#39; was lost and recreated with the same fields; its new id is task_ismqchob.&#10;(4) TextAnnotation names show in the outline but are saved as empty &#60;bpmn:textAnnotation/&#62; with no &#60;bpmn:text&#62;, and update notes is refused. Labels may be lost when the file is reopened." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_yw4idk04</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_vranm081</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_yw4idk04" sourceRef="task_n3u7jb5m" targetRef="task_w8q788dp" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_agaayr0l" name="Fix MCP apply_edits issues" dai:notes="2026-11-07: Paused ex-vector-craft-gen. Root causes are in ws-dai-studio/editor-src/src/embed/agentApi.ts:&#10;- add type bpmn:SubProcess builds a Task (TASKLIKE is mapped to bpmn:Task). It only became a container when a child was moved in, and then at 100x80, which cuts off content outside it.&#10;- add sets bo.name, but a TextAnnotation keeps its text in bo.text.&#10;- move treats parent &#34;&#34;/null as &#39;no change&#39;.&#10;- delete runs editing.remove, which also removes the container&#39;s children.&#10;- There&#39;s no way to size or resize a container.&#10;The tool schema is in app-dai-studio/src-tauri/src/mcp/tools.rs.&#10;Fixed in agentApi.ts / agentTypes.ts:&#10;- add keeps bpmn:SubProcess as a container (360x240) and takes size.&#10;- add writes TextAnnotation text to bo.text.&#10;- move with parent null/&#34;&#34; goes to the top level. Into a container without dx/dy, shapes keep their layout and go to its top-left. Containers grow to fit their content.&#10;- New resize op (x/y/width/height, or fit:true).&#10;- delete of a container with content is refused unless children is &#39;keep&#39; (move out first) or &#39;delete&#39;.&#10;Added 7 tests: editor 333/333, app 80/80, Rust MCP 18/18. tools.rs schema and server instructions updated, vendored editor rebuilt with make editor. Needs a DAI Studio restart to take effect. Not fixed: the large apply_edits batch failing to parse came from the client sending bad JSON, not from the server." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_vranm081</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_xtbmzv1h</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_vranm081" sourceRef="task_w8q788dp" targetRef="task_agaayr0l" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_ewd56n6d" name="Verify MCP fixes in running app" dai:notes="2026-11-07: Tested on the tauri dev build in the empty Untitled window, then deleted the test shapes. All 5 fixes work: SubProcess is added as a 360x240 container; moving into it places shapes at its top-left (+30,+40); parent:null moves to the top level; resize fit hugs the content; deleting a container with content is refused, and children:&#39;keep&#39; moves the content out and keeps its flow; annotation text is saved as &#60;bpmn:text&#62;.&#10;New issue: new_document and open_document fail with &#34;The document&#39;s window didn&#39;t finish loading. Is DAI Studio signed in?&#34; The .dai file is written, but its window never reports ready. Existing windows work fine.&#10;Correction: the window failure wasn&#39;t a sign-in problem. The test files were in /private/tmp (Claude&#39;s scratchpad), a path the editor can&#39;t read. The real problem is the misleading error message: it should say the path can&#39;t be reached, not ask about sign-in." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_xtbmzv1h</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_3z0tug0g</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_xtbmzv1h" sourceRef="task_agaayr0l" targetRef="task_ewd56n6d" />
    <bpmn:task id="task_nkzn484x" name="Clear errors for unreadable paths" dai:notes="2026-11-07: The window showed Tauri&#39;s &#34;forbidden path ... allow-read-text-file&#34; dialog, but MCP only timed out and suggested a sign-in problem. The window then fell back to a blank Untitled document, which MCP could have treated as the requested file.&#10;Fixes (app-dai-studio):&#10;- check_editor_can_read checks the real path against the fs scope roots (home, Documents, Desktop, Downloads) before opening a window. new_document runs it before writing anything.&#10;- New mcp_window_failed command. +page.svelte calls it before showing the error dialog.&#10;- wait_ready fails at once if the window reports an error or loads a different document.&#10;Verified live: new_document on /private/tmp failed immediately with the clear message, and no file was written. Tests: Rust 20/20 at the time." dai:agentStatus="done">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_3z0tug0g</bpmn:incoming>
