    <bpmn:task id="task_y7b9phzp" name="Play test in browser" dai:notes="2026-11-07: Serving the folder on localhost:8080 and playing it in Chrome with the claude-in-chrome tools: check the console, the overlay and HUD, terrain rendering, movement, breaking and placing, and that saves survive a reload.&#10;The claude-in-chrome extension wasn&#39;t connected, so I drove headless Chrome over the DevTools Protocol with a scratch script (Node 24 WebSocket). Results: no console errors; terrain loads and renders; standing, walking (5.5 blocks in 1.5s), jumping (1.39) and swimming work; break and place work and remesh; the save survives a reload; the underwater tint works. Fixes from the test: water alpha 0.62 → 0.8 with darker colours (shallow water read as ice), and an inline SVG favicon (the only 404). Added README.md. Not covered headless: real pointer-lock mouse look and clicks. The plan&#39;s Test task is set to passing, with the details in actualResult." dai:agentStatus="done" dai:planRef="task_0nvclp4r">
