    <bpmn:task id="task_jc1m97tx" name="Route row wraps bottom to top" dai:notes="2026-11-07: The user asked for the arrow that wraps to a new row to leave the bottom of the row&#39;s last step and enter the top of the next row&#39;s first step.&#10;- appendStep now gives a wrapping arrow a saved route (wrapRoute: down from the bottom centre, across the middle of the gap between rows, down into the top centre). Saved routes are marked manual, so they keep their shape when steps move.&#10;- apply_edits update takes waypoints for a connection, documented in tools.rs.&#10;- Tests: editor 334/334 (wrap route test and waypoints test added), Rust MCP 21/21.&#10;- Fixed this document&#39;s 2 existing wraps (flow_e2s337q8, flow_7fwfkmfr) with waypoints. They were already auto-routed bottom to top, but the second had a 1px kink (y 364 then 365)." dai:agentStatus="done">
